From 56e7cb0c952f3bd32020d21cda3a30904a03a212 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 11:54:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/23] gated_delta_net : rewrite chunked phase B, 33.8ms ->
 12.8ms

The old phase B (128 threads, 16 V-slices of 8) was latency-bound: serial
128-iteration reductions, shared inputs re-read per slice, and stride-8KB
global k loads in the state update. Rewrite with 256 threads and V-slices
of 32, one state column per thread so the 32 columns of a warp share every
kd/q/k/ac load as a warp broadcast (no L2 amplification):

- steps 1+2a merged: v_new = kcsum - kd @ S, o_q = q @ S, 8 token rows/thread
- step 3: S = P_last*S + (k .* delta)^T @ v_new, 16 state rows/thread with
  contiguous float2 k reads (k[t][k] is k-major; no transpose needed)
- s_S (16 KB) + s_vnew (8 KB) smem, 2 CTAs/CU, 1 wave (was 2)
- register-tiled 16x16 grid with smem staging was tried first: 192 VGPRs +
  spills (274 scratch instructions vs 308 FMAs in the ISA), 675us/launch;
  thread-per-column keeps live registers ~40 and hits 267us/launch

pp512 5436 -> 6068-6072 (sequential 5878); PPL 6.2426 (sequential 6.2572);
47/47 GATED_DELTA_NET tests. Docs: PERF_HANDOVER.md section 12.

Assisted-by: pi
